Licensing of the trained model weights in this directory
========================================================

The source code of DexteraAI is MIT licensed (see /LICENSE at the repository
root). The weights here are covered separately, because they are derived from
third-party training data whose terms differ from the code's. The two bundles do
not stand in the same place, so they are stated separately.


models/hagrid/  —  CC BY-SA 4.0
-------------------------------

Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You may use these weights for any purpose, including commercially. If you
distribute them or a work adapted from them, credit as below and license your
adaptation under CC BY-SA 4.0 or a compatible license.

This is not the project's preference; it is compliance. The weights are trained
on hand landmarks extracted from the HaGRID dataset, whose license requires that
adapted material carry "a license with the same License Elements […] or a
BY-SA-compatible license" (Section 3(b)(1)). CC BY-SA 4.0 is that license. Any
future bundle trained on data without a share-alike obligation can ship MIT with
the code.

    Trained on hand landmarks extracted from the HaGRID dataset by Alexander
    Kapitanov, Karina Kvanchiani, Alexander Nagaev, Roman Kraynov and Andrei
    Makhliarchuk (SberDevices).
      Dataset: https://github.com/hukenovs/hagrid
      License: https://github.com/hukenovs/hagrid/blob/master/license/en_us.pdf
      Paper:   https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.08219

    Changes made: no images are redistributed. A subset was read once to extract
    MediaPipe hand landmark coordinates, which were normalized into an
    86-dimensional feature vector and used as training input.

The dataset is provided by its licensors without warranties (Section 5 of that
license), and the same disclaimer carries to these weights.


models/asl_alphabet/  —  MIT, with attribution
--------------------------------------------

Licensed under the MIT License, the same as the code (see /LICENSE).

These weights are trained on hand landmarks extracted from **ASL-HG**, which is
CC BY 4.0: commercial use permitted, attribution required, and — unlike the
HaGRID licence covering the other bundle — no share-alike obligation. So there
is nothing here that has to stay open, and MIT is available.

    Trained on hand landmarks extracted from the ASL-HG dataset by Md. Famidul
    Islam Pranto, Md. Rifatul Islam, Md. Ali Akbor, Nabonita Ghosh, Md. Rahatun
    Alam, Sudipto Chaki and Md Masudul Islam (Bangladesh University of Business
    and Technology).
      Dataset: https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/j4y5w2c8w9/1
      Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0
      DOI:     10.17632/j4y5w2c8w9.1

    Changes made: images are not redistributed. A subset was read once to
    extract MediaPipe hand landmark coordinates, which were normalised into an
    86-dimensional feature vector and used as training input. The two-handed
    "0" class was excluded, this pipeline encoding a single hand.

This replaces an earlier bundle trained on a HuggingFace re-upload that
declared no licence at all, and which therefore could not be licensed onward.
That bundle is gone rather than relicensed.
